# LaunchKit — Cursor Rules
# Version: Milestone 3 (AI-First)

You are working on LaunchKit, a production-ready SaaS starter kit.

## Tech Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router, Server Components, Server Actions)
- **Language**: TypeScript 5.6 (strict mode — no `any`, no type assertions without justification)
- **Database**: Neon Postgres (serverless) + Drizzle ORM ^0.36
- **Auth**: Clerk (multi-tenant, orgs, webhooks)
- **Billing**: Stripe only (Apple Pay, Google Pay, Link via Checkout)
- **UI**: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui + Radix primitives
- **AI**: Vercel AI SDK (openai, anthropic, google providers)
- **Email**: React Email + Resend
- **Repo**: Turborepo + pnpm workspaces

## Monorepo Structure

```
apps/
  web/                    ← Next.js application (main app)
    app/                  ← Next.js App Router
      api/ai/             ← AI API routes (chat, summarize, generate, images, documents, search)
      api/billing/        ← Checkout + portal routes
      api/webhooks/       ← Stripe + Clerk webhook handlers
      dashboard/          ← Protected dashboard pages
      settings/           ← User settings pages
      auth/               ← Sign-in / sign-up pages
    components/
      ai/                 ← AI feature components (chat, etc.)
      dashboard/          ← Header, sidebar
      ui/                 ← shadcn/ui primitives (button, card, input, etc.)
      shared/             ← Theme provider, theme toggle
    lib/
      credits.ts          ← getCredits, deductCredits, addCredits
      rag.ts              ← chunkText, generateEmbedding, indexDocument, searchDocuments
      stripe.ts           ← Stripe client (lazy-initialized)
      utils.ts            ← cn() utility

packages/
  database/               ← Drizzle ORM schema, client, migrations
    src/schema/           ← Table definitions (users, orgs, subscriptions, credits, ai-chats, documents)
    drizzle.config.ts     ← Drizzle Kit config
    src/seed.ts           ← Database seed script
  config/                 ← Site and billing plan configuration
    src/plans.ts          ← Plan definitions (free, pro, team) with Stripe + LS price IDs
    src/site.ts           ← siteConfig object
  email/                  ← React Email templates + Resend
    src/templates/        ← welcome.tsx, team-invite.tsx
    src/index.ts          ← sendEmail(), template exports
  mcp-server/             ← MCP server for AI coding assistants
    src/index.ts          ← All tool definitions and handlers
    src/tasks/            ← send-welcome-email, send-team-invite, sync-billing-seats, etc.
    src/index.ts          ← All job exports
  tsconfig/               ← Shared TypeScript configs
```

## The 7 Golden Rules

1. **Server Components by default.** Never add `"use client"` unless you need hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`), event handlers, or browser APIs (`window`, `localStorage`). Forms using Server Actions do NOT need `"use client"`.

2. **Clerk for all auth.** Server: `import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server"`. Client: `useUser()`, `useOrganization()`. Never roll custom auth.

3. **Drizzle ORM for all DB.** Import from `@launchkit/database`. Use `db.query.*` for reads, `db.insert/update/delete` for writes. Never use raw SQL strings.

4. **shadcn/ui for all UI.** Components are in `components/ui/`. Add new shadcn components with `npx shadcn@latest add [component]`. Always use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.

5. **Zod for all validation.** Validate all API inputs, form inputs, and environment variables with Zod schemas.

6. **Credits before AI.** Every AI operation must check `getCredits()` and call `deductCredits()`. CREDIT_COST constants: chat=1, summarize=2, generate=2, image=10, embedding=1.

7. **No module-scope initialization.** Never call `new OpenAI()`, `new Stripe()`, or `neon()` at the top level. Always use lazy-init patterns (see patterns below).

## File Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Pages | `app/[route]/page.tsx` | `app/dashboard/reports/page.tsx` |
| Layouts | `app/[route]/layout.tsx` | `app/dashboard/layout.tsx` |
| Loading states | `app/[route]/loading.tsx` | `app/dashboard/loading.tsx` |
| API routes | `app/api/[route]/route.ts` | `app/api/ai/chat/route.ts` |
| Components | `components/[domain]/[name].tsx` | `components/dashboard/stats-card.tsx` |
| Utilities | `lib/[name].ts` | `lib/credits.ts` |
| Hooks | `hooks/use-[name].ts` | `hooks/use-credits.ts` |
| Types | `types/[name].ts` | `types/billing.ts` |

## Component Pattern

```tsx
// components/dashboard/stats-card.tsx
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

interface StatsCardProps {
  title: string;
  value: string | number;
  description?: string;
  className?: string;
}

export function StatsCard({ title, value, description, className }: StatsCardProps) {
  return (
    <div className={cn("rounded-lg border bg-card p-6", className)}>
      <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{title}</p>
      <p className="text-3xl font-bold">{value}</p>
      {description && <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{description}</p>}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Page Pattern (Server Component)

```tsx
// app/dashboard/reports/page.tsx
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { redirect } from "next/navigation";
import { db } from "@launchkit/database";

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: "Reports",
  description: "View your analytics and usage reports",
};

export default async function ReportsPage() {
  const { userId, orgId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) redirect("/auth/sign-in");

  const data = await db.query.users.findFirst({ where: eq(users.id, userId) });

  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      <h1 className="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Reports</h1>
      {/* Content */}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## API Route Pattern

```typescript
// app/api/example/route.ts
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { z } from "zod";
import { db } from "@launchkit/database";

const Schema = z.object({
  field: z.string().min(1),
});

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { userId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) return Response.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });

  const body = await req.json();
  const parsed = Schema.safeParse(body);
  if (!parsed.success) return Response.json({ error: parsed.error.flatten() }, { status: 422 });

  try {
    // business logic
    return Response.json({ data: result });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("[api/example/POST]", error);
    return Response.json({ error: "Internal server error" }, { status: 500 });
  }
}
```

## AI API Route Pattern

```typescript
import { streamText } from "ai";
import { openai } from "@ai-sdk/openai";
import { auth } from "@clerk/nextjs/server";
import { deductCredits, getCredits } from "@/lib/credits";

const CREDIT_COST = 1;

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { userId, orgId } = await auth();
  if (!userId) return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });

  const balance = await getCredits(userId);
  if (balance < CREDIT_COST) {
    return Response.json({ error: "Insufficient credits" }, { status: 402 });
  }

  await deductCredits(userId, CREDIT_COST, "AI operation description");

  const result = streamText({
    model: openai("gpt-4o"),
    messages,
    onFinish: async ({ usage }) => {
      if (orgId) await reportAIUsage(orgId, usage?.totalTokens ?? 1);
    },
  });

  return result.toDataStreamResponse();
}
```

## Database Pattern

```typescript
// Reading data
import { db } from "@launchkit/database";
import { users, organizations } from "@launchkit/database";
import { eq, and, desc } from "drizzle-orm";

const user = await db.query.users.findFirst({
  where: eq(users.clerkId, userId),
  with: { memberships: true },
});

// Writing data
await db.insert(documents).values({ organizationId, title, content });
await db.update(users).set({ name }).where(eq(users.id, userId));
await db.delete(documents).where(eq(documents.id, documentId));
```

## Adding a New Table

1. Create `packages/database/src/schema/[table-name].ts`
2. Export from `packages/database/src/schema/index.ts`
3. Run `pnpm db:generate` to create migration
4. Run `pnpm db:migrate` to apply it

## Lazy-Init Patterns (Required for External Services)

```typescript
// ✅ Correct — lazy initialization
let _openai: OpenAI | null = null;
function getOpenAI() {
  if (!_openai) _openai = new OpenAI({ apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY });
  return _openai;
}

// ✅ Also correct — Proxy pattern (used for db client)
export const db = new Proxy({} as Database, {
  get(_target, prop, receiver) {
    const instance = getDb();
    return Reflect.get(instance, prop, receiver);
  },
});

// ❌ Wrong — module-scope initialization (breaks serverless cold starts)
const openai = new OpenAI({ apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY });
```

## Credit Costs Reference

| Operation | Credits |
|-----------|---------|
| AI Chat (per request) | 1 |
| Summarize | 2 |
| Content Generation | 2 |
| Image (DALL-E 3) | 10 |
| Document Embedding (per chunk) | 1 |
| Semantic Search | 1 |

## Plan Limits Reference

| Plan | Credits/month | Seats | Price |
|------|--------------|-------|-------|
| Free | 100 | 1 | $0 |
| Pro | 5,000 | 5 | $29/mo |
| Team | 25,000 | 25 | $79/mo |

## Billing Adapter

The billing provider is abstracted. To add billing logic:
- Check `process.env.BILLING_PROVIDER` (default: `"stripe"`)
- Use `packages/config/src/plans.ts` for plan definitions
- Stripe webhooks: `app/api/webhooks/stripe/route.ts`
- Always verify webhook signatures before processing


## RAG / Document Search

```typescript
import { indexDocument, searchDocuments } from "@/lib/rag";

// Index a document (background: use process-document-embedding job for large docs)
await indexDocument(orgId, "Title", content, { metadata: { source: "upload" } });

// Semantic search
const results = await searchDocuments(orgId, "user query", 5);
// results: Array<{ id, title, content, similarity, metadata, chunkIndex }>
```

## Testing

- E2E tests with Playwright: `pnpm test:e2e` (from apps/web)
- Test files live alongside pages or in a `__tests__` directory
- Always use `@playwright/test` — not Jest for E2E

## Common Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| `auth()` not called before DB query | Always call `auth()` first in server code |
| Module-scope `new OpenAI()` | Use lazy-init with a getter function |
| Using `any` type | Use `unknown` + type guards, or proper types |
| Missing `"use client"` on interactive component | Add when using hooks/events |
| Missing credit check before AI op | Always `getCredits()` + `deductCredits()` first |
| SQL injection risk | Use Drizzle parameterized queries, never `sql\`...\`` with user input |
| Hardcoded env var | Always use `process.env.VAR_NAME` |

## Don't

- Don't use `getServerSession` — use Clerk's `auth()` instead
- Don't use Prisma — use Drizzle ORM
- Don't create new UI primitives — use shadcn/ui components
- Don't hardcode secrets — use environment variables from `.env.local`
- Don't use `any` type — use strict TypeScript
- Don't initialize clients at module scope — use lazy-init patterns
- Don't skip auth checks in API routes
- Don't skip credit checks before AI operations
- Don't use CSS modules or styled-components — use Tailwind only
- Don't bypass the billing abstraction — always use `BILLING_PROVIDER`
